406beba50b23a642784ec5cb406c933f6f6ba7898445ce1d8210d72a7840dfb4[{"version":1,"source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-038674","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001966678","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966678/000149315226038674/form20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81.bin","sha256":"48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81"},"layers":{"businessProfile":{"status":"evidence_available","evidence":[{"id":"1566b4180177b2b54408686634266908536e74547b31e25c29de928932be4170","quote":"We are a holding company incorporated under the laws of the Cayman Islands on April 14, 2022. Our wholly-owned direct subsidiary is Celestial Power, a British Virgin Islands holding company incorporated on February 22, 2022. We operate our business through Primega Construction, our Hong Kong subsidiary incorporated on July 31, 2018, which is wholly owned by Celestial Power. Primega Construction is principally engaged in soil and rock transportation services in Hong Kong.","context":"A. History and Development of the Company.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":429,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-038674","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001966678","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966678/000149315226038674/form20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81.bin","sha256":"48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81"}},{"id":"cc04e68dc831e9361307ca8124be8d90c4b8426829fcd40805a53fb42ef33ebb","quote":"In February 2022, Celestial Power was incorporated under the laws of the BVI as the intermediate holding company of ZDAI. One (1) share of Celestial Power, representing its entire issued share capital, was allotted and issued to ZDAI on May 4, 2022.","context":"We are a holding company incorporated under the laws of the Cayman Islands on April 14, 2022. Our wholly-owned direct subsidiary is Celestial Power, a British Virgin Islands holding company incorporated on February 22, 2022. We operate our business through Primega Construction, our Hong Kong subsidiary incorporated on July 31, 2018, which is wholly owned by Celestial Power. Primega Construction is principally engaged in soil and rock transportation services in Hong Kong.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":430,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-038674","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001966678","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966678/000149315226038674/form20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81.bin","sha256":"48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81"}},{"id":"22b67103dc2809903de71aafdc4e118f77ab4b9e737f7b22ef7fce5f36461792","quote":"In April 2022, ZDAI was incorporated under the laws of the Cayman Islands as an exempted company with limited liability, as the holding company of our BVI and Hong Kong subsidiary.","context":"In February 2022, Celestial Power was incorporated under the laws of the BVI as the intermediate holding company of ZDAI. One (1) share of Celestial Power, representing its entire issued share capital, was allotted and issued to ZDAI on May 4, 2022.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":431,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-038674","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001966678","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966678/000149315226038674/form20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81.bin","sha256":"48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81"}},{"id":"8ab72e10366c2ce11e4d1d2ac93bb5ac5692f8f33a017e3528fddca7b7c827a9","quote":"In June 2022, as part of a reorganization, ZDAI acquired, through Celestial Power, all the shares of Primega Construction from Mr. Man Siu Ming and became the ultimate holding company of Celestial Power and Primega Construction. On April 14, 2022, ZDAI issued 11,249,999 ordinary shares to Mr. Man Siu Ming.","context":"In April 2022, ZDAI was incorporated under the laws of the Cayman Islands as an exempted company with limited liability, as the holding company of our BVI and Hong Kong subsidiary.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":432,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-038674","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001966678","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966678/000149315226038674/form20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81.bin","sha256":"48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81"}},{"id":"e807661fb6d0f09755d976c1afa1fb66c2df3577057212f74f7db9e765957dfa","quote":"On July 20, 2022, the Mr. Man Siu Ming sold 551,250 ordinary shares each to Primewin Corporate Development Limited and Shun Kai Investment Development Limited. Primewin Corporate Development Limited and Shun Kai Investment Development Limited are wholly owned by Mr. Lau Wing Him Perry and Mr. Chan Wan Yiu, respectively. Primewin Corporate Development Limited was one of our major customers for the year ended March 31, 2021. Mr. Chan Wan Yiu is an employee of Primega Construction, our Hong Kong operating subsidiary.","context":"In June 2022, as part of a reorganization, ZDAI acquired, through Celestial Power, all the shares of Primega Construction from Mr. Man Siu Ming and became the ultimate holding company of Celestial Power and Primega Construction. On April 14, 2022, ZDAI issued 11,249,999 ordinary shares to Mr. Man Siu Ming.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":433,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-038674","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001966678","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966678/000149315226038674/form20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81.bin","sha256":"48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81"}},{"id":"a31f5b03fb2061bd69dad9c11a8f48008cb65b9f8d41e08de8c10f4ff6ca7865","quote":"On December 5, 2023, Mr. Man Siu Ming entered into individual sale and purchase agreements with each of Dusk Moon International Limited and Moss Mist Investment Limited. Pursuant to these agreements, Mr. Man Siu Ming agreed to sell, and each of Dusk Moon International Limited and Moss Mist Investment Limited agreed to purchase, 551,250 ordinary shares.","context":"On July 20, 2022, the Mr. Man Siu Ming sold 551,250 ordinary shares each to Primewin Corporate Development Limited and Shun Kai Investment Development Limited. Primewin Corporate Development Limited and Shun Kai Investment Development Limited are wholly owned by Mr. Lau Wing Him Perry and Mr. Chan Wan Yiu, respectively. Primewin Corporate Development Limited was one of our major customers for the year ended March 31, 2021. Mr. Chan Wan Yiu is an employee of Primega Construction, our Hong Kong operating subsidiary.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":434,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-038674","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001966678","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966678/000149315226038674/form20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81.bin","sha256":"48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81"}},{"id":"ea5fb15c687cacda3dc2a54a16344c4cbe97070542f178306294fa8587db9805","quote":"As part of the series of reorganization transactions to be completed before the IPO, a 2-for-1 share split was conducted by the Company on February 28, 2024. After the share split, the authorized share capital of the Company consists of US$50,000 divided into 1,000,000,000 ordinary shares, par value US$0.00005 each (US$0.0008, after giving effect to the share consolidation), and the issued share capital of the Company then consisted of US$1,125 divided into 22,500,000 ordinary shares, par value of US$0.00005 each.","context":"On December 5, 2023, Mr. Man Siu Ming entered into individual sale and purchase agreements with each of Dusk Moon International Limited and Moss Mist Investment Limited. Pursuant to these agreements, Mr. Man Siu Ming agreed to sell, and each of Dusk Moon International Limited and Moss Mist Investment Limited agreed to purchase, 551,250 ordinary shares.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":435,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-038674","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001966678","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966678/000149315226038674/form20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81.bin","sha256":"48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81"}},{"id":"23214239a8613838a2627401f3b38809d8967738405c8e30bf0472ea4afd26e0","quote":"On September 12, 2025, we changed our name to DirectBooking Technology Co., Ltd. and adopted the dual foreign name “直订科技有限公司”.","context":"As part of the series of reorganization transactions to be completed before the IPO, a 2-for-1 share split was conducted by the Company on February 28, 2024. After the share split, the authorized share capital of the Company consists of US$50,000 divided into 1,000,000,000 ordinary shares, par value US$0.00005 each (US$0.0008, after giving effect to the share consolidation), and the issued share capital of the Company then consisted of US$1,125 divided into 22,500,000 ordinary shares, par value of US$0.00005 each.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":436,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-038674","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001966678","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966678/000149315226038674/form20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81.bin","sha256":"48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81"}},{"id":"fcb8354b5c50493c30395eaa682d8a0e0146564a0953bc685bff376a958de83e","quote":"Our ordinary shares commenced trading on the Nasdaq Capital Market on July 23, 2024. On May 16, 2025, our trading symbol was changed from “PGHL” to “ZDAI”.","context":"On September 12, 2025, we changed our name to DirectBooking Technology Co., Ltd. and adopted the dual foreign name “直订科技有限公司”.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":437,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-038674","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001966678","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966678/000149315226038674/form20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81.bin","sha256":"48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81"}},{"id":"e56031aeb1202c31cf6fff31e291770b9d7b27b8a4e80dde3d19fb3e0131f6be","quote":"On July 16, 2025, Tan Yu was appointed as our Chief Executive Officer and Liu Wei was appointed as our Chief Financial Officer. We also experienced changes in the composition of our board of directors and board committees, as more fully described in “Item 6. Directors, Senior Management and Employees.”","context":"Our ordinary shares commenced trading on the Nasdaq Capital Market on July 23, 2024. On May 16, 2025, our trading symbol was changed from “PGHL” to “ZDAI”.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":438,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-038674","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001966678","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966678/000149315226038674/form20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81.bin","sha256":"48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81"}},{"id":"0148a949ec4f5fbf3e3c23f298fc883aec16ea931599088d9b159672c4ffa0a8","quote":"On August 19, 2025, the Company entered into a Memorandum of Understanding (the “MOU”), dated August 18, 2025. Pursuant to the MOU, on November 11, 2025, the Company entered into a securities purchase agreement (the “SPA”) for the purchase of 49% of the total issued shares of China Wangmao. The Company paid the total purchase price of approximately US$12.7 million in or about December 2025 in accordance with the terms of the SPA. However, due to commercial considerations and unforeseen events, the Company has not yet received any shares of China Wangmao.","context":"On July 16, 2025, Tan Yu was appointed as our Chief Executive Officer and Liu Wei was appointed as our Chief Financial Officer. We also experienced changes in the composition of our board of directors and board committees, as more fully described in “Item 6. Directors, Senior Management and Employees.”","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":439,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-038674","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001966678","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966678/000149315226038674/form20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81.bin","sha256":"48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81"}},{"id":"4bd6d3484d4a4fedf0ce75dfbf2c7f0a8143cbc7613606cf1436132bc32de437","quote":"On December 14, 2025, our shareholders approved, among other matters, changes to our authorized share capital, the adoption of an amended and restated memorandum and articles of association, and authorization for a reverse share split and share reclassification. On January 23, 2026, our board approved a 16-for-1 reverse share split, which became effective on February 17, 2026. Following the reverse share split, the par value of each of our Class A Ordinary Shares and Class B Ordinary Shares became US$0.0008 per share. All share and per share amounts in the accompanying consolidated financial statements and notes have been retroactively adjusted to reflect the effects of the reverse stock splits, including rounding of fractional shares to whole shares where applicable.","context":"On August 19, 2025, the Company entered into a Memorandum of Understanding (the “MOU”), dated August 18, 2025. Pursuant to the MOU, on November 11, 2025, the Company entered into a securities purchase agreement (the “SPA”) for the purchase of 49% of the total issued shares of China Wangmao. The Company paid the total purchase price of approximately US$12.7 million in or about December 2025 in accordance with the terms of the SPA. However, due to commercial considerations and unforeseen events, the Company has not yet received any shares of China Wangmao.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":440,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-038674","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001966678","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966678/000149315226038674/form20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81.bin","sha256":"48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81"}},{"id":"d670ccae5522b42b60360fec06aa3c0409f66d3d480468f01a3305391496f9c8","quote":"On March 25, 2026, our shareholders approved certain additional resolutions relating to our capital structure, including an increase in authorized share capital, amendments to the voting rights of our Class B Ordinary Shares, and the adoption of our third amended and restated memorandum and articles of association (the “Third Memorandum and Articles of Association” or the “Memorandum and Articles of Association”). See “Item 10. Additional Information—B. Memorandum and Articles of Association.”","context":"Table of Contents","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":443,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-038674","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001966678","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966678/000149315226038674/form20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81.bin","sha256":"48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81"}},{"id":"b1a0dd8b6444786cf32a6c69a2f8044541731f32d5fc0ed95a42c31e1a1fc44b","quote":"On July 21, 2026, we entered into a strategic joint venture agreement with Beijing DeepYou Digital Technology Co., Ltd. (“DeepYou”). Under the agreement, DirectBooking will hold a 51% equity interest in the joint venture and DeepYou will hold 49%.","context":"On March 25, 2026, our shareholders approved certain additional resolutions relating to our capital structure, including an increase in authorized share capital, amendments to the voting rights of our Class B Ordinary Shares, and the adoption of our third amended and restated memorandum and articles of association (the “Third Memorandum and Articles of Association” or the “Memorandum and Articles of Association”). See “Item 10. Additional Information—B. Memorandum and Articles of Association.”","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":444,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-038674","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001966678","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966678/000149315226038674/form20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81.bin","sha256":"48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81"}},{"id":"692fdb67afd847ce14ec5652b41b71134372eb06be43a65b833d8f9b374c29ed","quote":"The two parties agreed to jointly establish a new technology company to build China’s first natively Agent-to-Agent, fully integrated travel-and-stay next-generation AI direct-booking platform for the hospitality sector. The platform will provide robotic staff solutions for hospitality enterprises on the enterprise side and robotic assistant services for users on the consumer side.","context":"On July 21, 2026, we entered into a strategic joint venture agreement with Beijing DeepYou Digital Technology Co., Ltd. (“DeepYou”). Under the agreement, DirectBooking will hold a 51% equity interest in the joint venture and DeepYou will hold 49%.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":445,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-038674","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001966678","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966678/000149315226038674/form20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81.bin","sha256":"48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81"}},{"id":"c33147dbdc502f3b636f7c41fd529f24d7ea2b952a75cb77c415a7b642932590","quote":"The project has set a three-year strategic target: for the AI travel and hospitality direct-booking platform to cover 30,000 to 50,000 hotels, and to provide each hotel with 3 to 10 AI “employees” to reduce operating costs while significantly improving efficiency and user experience. At the same time, through AI-driven innovation, the project aims to break the traditional OTA industry’s channel monopoly and information silos, reshape value distribution across the industry, and build a more open and inclusive industrial ecosystem.","context":"The two parties agreed to jointly establish a new technology company to build China’s first natively Agent-to-Agent, fully integrated travel-and-stay next-generation AI direct-booking platform for the hospitality sector. The platform will provide robotic staff solutions for hospitality enterprises on the enterprise side and robotic assistant services for users on the consumer side.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":446,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-038674","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001966678","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966678/000149315226038674/form20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81.bin","sha256":"48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81"}},{"id":"a03b8ebd4034a004b3cb6092f90a5bc0b33eb416ab185be88b28a0b16db6ea4f","quote":"Regarding the Prepayment for investment in China Wangmao Liquor Industry Group Co., Limited, on August 11, 2026, the Company and China Wangmao mutually agreed to terminate the SPA effective immediately. Pursuant to the termination terms, China Wangmao agreed to refund the full principal amount of US$12,700,000 and pay compensatory interest at an annual rate of 5.25% for the period during which it held the purchase price. On August 13, 2026, the Company fully recovered the principal amount of USD12.7 million together with all accrued interest in cash.","context":"The project has set a three-year strategic target: for the AI travel and hospitality direct-booking platform to cover 30,000 to 50,000 hotels, and to provide each hotel with 3 to 10 AI “employees” to reduce operating costs while significantly improving efficiency and user experience. At the same time, through AI-driven innovation, the project aims to break the traditional OTA industry’s channel monopoly and information silos, reshape value distribution across the industry, and build a more open and inclusive industrial ecosystem.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":447,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-038674","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001966678","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966678/000149315226038674/form20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81.bin","sha256":"48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81"}},{"id":"98b3e2602ebb391accbbde5ef73d4f825d529089cc3d8fbad739524565a70126","quote":"Our agent for service of process in the United States is Cogency Global Inc., located at 122 East 42nd Street, 18th Floor New York, NY 10168.","context":"Regarding the Prepayment for investment in China Wangmao Liquor Industry Group Co., Limited, on August 11, 2026, the Company and China Wangmao mutually agreed to terminate the SPA effective immediately. Pursuant to the termination terms, China Wangmao agreed to refund the full principal amount of US$12,700,000 and pay compensatory interest at an annual rate of 5.25% for the period during which it held the purchase price. On August 13, 2026, the Company fully recovered the principal amount of USD12.7 million together with all accrued interest in cash.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":448,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-038674","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001966678","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966678/000149315226038674/form20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81.bin","sha256":"48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81"}},{"id":"dcac3a069e0ded018f93bf49a7af0a7c8299fee998290defa72d25e23e4c42d9","quote":"SEC maintains an internet site that contains reports, proxy and information statements, and other information regarding issuers that file electronically with the SEC on www.sec.gov. You can also find information on our website http://www.primegagroup.com. Information contained on, or that can be accessed through, our website is not a part of, and shall not be incorporated by reference into, this annual report.","context":"Our agent for service of process in the United States is Cogency Global Inc., located at 122 East 42nd Street, 18th Floor New York, NY 10168.","section":"Item 4. Information on the Company","block":449,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-038674","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik