edings, or where long-aged receivables remain unpaid despite repeated collection efforts, whichever occurs earlier.","context":"Irrespective of the outcome of the above assessment, the Company presumes that the credit risk has increased significantly for those outstanding balance aged over 1 year, unless the Company has reasonable and supportable information that demonstrates otherwise.","section":"Segment Reporting","block":1464,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-038674","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001966678","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966678/000149315226038674/form20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81.bin","sha256":"48ef7e74a66e3abaf3748ca9820fc3a51b90cea4191289c31f2b1557e1db1c81"}},{"id":"967fa18c0f1420f1e56cdfa7c300cc9aea46d5a1543b7683c4648b4fb24d2ef7","quote":"On August 19, 2025, the Company entered into a Memorandum of Understanding (the “MOU”), dated August 18, 2025. Pursuant to the MOU, on November 11, 2025, the Company entered into a securities purchase agreement (the “SPA”) for the purchase of 49% of the total issued shares of China Wangmao. The Company paid the total purchase price of approximately US$12.7 million in or about December 2025 in accordance with the terms of the SPA. However, due to commercial considerations and unforeseen events, the Company has not yet received any shares of China Wangmao.","context":"Prepayment for investment in China Wangmao Liquor Industry Group Co., Limited (“China Wangmao”)","section":"Segment Reporting","block":1477,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-038674","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-08-17","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001966678","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data